{
  "dom_id": "step-q154915",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "If ${a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}-3$ with ${a}_{1}=-1,$ then ${a}_{3}=$",
  "worked_solution": "The recursive formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}={a}_{n}-3,\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}=-1.$\n\nWe use this formula to compute the terms ${a}_{2}$ and ${a}_{3}$ as follows:\n\n- We first compute ${a}_{2}$ by substituting $n=1$ into the recursive formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n+1} & ={a}_{n}-3 \\\\ {a}_{1+1} & ={a}_{1}-3 \\\\ {a}_{2} & ={a}_{1}-3 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =(-1)-3 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we compute ${a}_{3}$ by substituting $n=2$ into the recursive formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n+1} & ={a}_{n}-3 \\\\ {a}_{2+1} & ={a}_{2}-3 \\\\ {a}_{3} & ={a}_{2}-3 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =(-4)-3 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${a}_{3}=-7.$",
